      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgetown%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Georgetown sits at the junction of Bradley, Hamilton, and Meigs counties, making it an unincorporated community that straddles three county lines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgetown%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community lies along State Route 60, near where the historic Trail of Tears crossed Tennessee in 1838.",
